{
  "_comment": "CLETS-001 is filed with every request - DV-100 page 13 lists it as one of the three forms the filer must complete - so it is activated unconditionally. Most of what it asks about is already in the packet under the packet's own names, and travels: the two people's names, the filer's age, and the four other protected people. What is left is the identifying detail only a law-enforcement database wants, which is what this interview asks for. The form stars the required fields; everything else it calls helpful, so the optional ones say so rather than pressing for an answer.",
